    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Students Pickup Planning</h1>
    <p>A student's pickup day is the semester's quiet milestone, the day the transport question resolves into a set of keys, and it rewards exactly the kind of planning students are supposedly bad at: a class-free hour, a written question list, a daylight walkaround and a first week of honest rehearsal. The visit happens at the shop's verified counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, inside opening hours of 09:00 to 21:00 daily, and the plan's whole job is to make that one visit found the term properly: the right machine confirmed, the paperwork asked, the baseline photographed and the riding life started calmly. This page builds the plan on verified facts only, with no promised delivery and no invented pickup arrangements.</p>
    <p>The page is part of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster, written for students. The verified fleet prices sit on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the questions the visit should ask are collected in the student paperwork guide in this cluster.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">The pickup, planned like a good study week</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Choosing the hour around the timetable</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Getting there and getting home</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">The counter conversation, list in hand</a></li>
